From: tcpcc project <tcpcc@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] init: add a post-kernel-init architecture hook

Hosted architectures can have no userspace init process while still needing
normal kernel_init() finalization, including free_initmem(), SYSTEM_RUNNING,
and the end of in-kernel RCU boot.  Add a no-op architecture hook after those
steps and before Linux starts trying userspace init paths.

Normal architectures retain identical behavior.  ARCH=tcpcc overrides the
hook to enter its long-lived host-control runtime only after normal boot
finalization has completed.

---
 init/main.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/init/main.c b/init/main.c
--- a/init/main.c
+++ b/init/main.c
@@ -1422,6 +1422,11 @@ void __weak free_initmem(void)
 	free_initmem_default(POISON_FREE_INITMEM);
 }
 
+void __weak arch_post_kernel_init(void)
+{
+}
+
 static int __ref kernel_init(void *unused)
 {
 	int ret;
@@ -1458,6 +1463,8 @@ static int __ref kernel_init(void *unused)
 
 	do_sysctl_args();
 
+	arch_post_kernel_init();
+
 	if (ramdisk_execute_command) {
 		ret = run_init_process(ramdisk_execute_command);
 		if (!ret)
-- 
